{"xson":[{"/iati-activities/iati-activity":[{"/activity-date":[{"@iso-date":"2010-04-22","@type":"2"},{"@iso-date":"2018-07-31","@type":"4"}],"/activity-status@code":"4","/collaboration-type@code":"2","/contact-info":[{"/department/narrative":[{"1":"WCA","@xml:lang":"EN"}],"/email":[{"1":"e.rwabidadi@ifad.org"}],"/job-title/narrative":[{"1":"Head of MCO/Country Director","@xml:lang":"EN"}],"/organisation/narrative":[{"1":"International Fund for Agricultural Development","@xml:lang":"EN"}],"/person-name/narrative":[{"1":"Rwabidadi, Eric","@xml:lang":"EN"}],"/telephone":[{"1":"+390654591"}],"/website":[{"1":"http://www.ifad.org"}],"@type":"1"}],"/default-aid-type":[{"@code":"C01","@vocabulary":"1"}],"/default-tied-status@code":"5","/description":[{"/narrative":[{"1":"Key project objectives12.The overall goal of the project is to reduce poverty, increase income and improve food security of the target group through the enhanced competitiveness of locally produced rice and onions. More specifically, the project aims to: (i) increase the production of rice and onions; (ii) improve the conservation, processing and marketing of the target commodities; and (iii) strengthen the technical and organisational capacity of rice and onion smallholders.Policy and institutional objectives13.The project will work on improving the enabling policy and institutional environment for the development of rice and onion value chains. The stakeholders including farmers' organizations, processors, traders and government will tackle issues such as taxes on imported rice and onions, pricing policy, norms and standards, roadblocks and illegal taxes on inputs and outputs","@xml:lang":"EN"}]}],"/document-link":[{"/category":[{"@code":"A12"}],"/description/narrative":[{"1":"More information on how IFAD publish IATI data to ensure the effectiveness of development.","@xml:lang":"EN"}],"/language":[{"@code":"EN"}],"/title/narrative":[{"1":"IATI documentation on IFAD corporate website","@xml:lang":"EN"}]